  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Simplified simulation: no air resistance, and the ball starts at ground level on flat ground.",
    "Gravity is 9.8 m/s² straight down; the sideways speed stays constant and only the vertical speed changes.",
    "Every point of the flight comes from the exact projectile formulas, so the landing distance equals speed² × sin(2 × angle) ÷ 9.8.",
    "The ball is a point for the physics (drawn as a ball for visibility); the flight ends when it returns to ground height.",
    "Each flight is shown over 2 seconds whatever its real flight time; the flight-time readout gives the real time.",
    "Targets come in a fixed order (30 m, 45 m, 18 m); Reset starts the same challenge again and clears the score and arcs."
  ],
